heres the actual pipeline of bm25s tokenization:

document is an object that contains plain text with its metada
we used a function to unpack content and metadata

1- tokenize

we take the content, thats plain text
and pass to bm25s to tokenize it
--> bm25s returns a toknize object with 2 elements: ids and vocab

2- tokenizising process:

a-
we take the content, then split it into tokens
"# Contributing to vLLM"  →  ["#", "contributing", "vllm"]
still strings here!!


b-
build vocab table
vocab is about finding unique tokens, then assign them IDS
then replace every token its ID

encoding is the process by which we take the string_word and convert it to ID
text  →  tokens  →  [ENCODING]  →  IDs
         (words)     (vocab)      (numbers)

encodingn is what turns our tokens_words to IDs

====================================

process:

content = ["hello world", "world peace"]
        │
        ▼  1. split into tokens
tokens = [["hello", "world"], ["world", "peace"]]
        │
        ▼  2. build vocab (scan all tokens, find unique ones, assign IDs)
vocab = {"hello": 0, "world": 1, "peace": 2}
        │
        ▼  3. encode (lookup each token)
ids = [[0, 1], [1, 2]]

